  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `connected_pieces` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/unreached.rs` reads each outer loop with `Region::from_slices`. Before, it used `Region::new`.\n- A loop that crosses itself is now read as its even-odd lobes. The check does not stop.\n- The noise filters of the check are the same (`PIECE_AREA_MIN`, `SLIVER_HALF_WIDTH`, `CORNER_HALF_WIDTH`).\n- `docs/decisions/2849-corner-cusp-loop.md` records the decision.\n\nThis PR is partial work for #2849. It fixes the defect that the issue names (\"loop crosses itself\" in the corner check). It does not change the three toolpath tests of the issue.\n\n## Cause\n\n- `unreached_corners` computes `leftover = piece.difference(&swept)`. Then it calls `connected_pieces(&leftover)`.\n- A bore drawn as chords leaves a cusp a few microns wide at each chord vertex.\n- On the micron lattice, the boolean can return such a cusp as one loop that crosses itself.\n- `Region::new` refuses that loop. The error stopped the whole corner check.\n- The user then saw only the note \"the check for corners of the stock tighter than the tool did not run (invalid geometry: loop crosses itself)\".\n- The defect does not need the solidcore importer. It is on `main` for a synthetic bore.\n\n## Tests\n\nPin: `machining2d::unreached::law::a_chord_cusp_that_crosses_itself_does_not_stop_the_corner_check` (`camcraft-motion`, lib).\n\n- The pin builds a 25 mm bore with 50, 60 and 63 chords. The reach is 2, 3 and 4 mm.\n- It asserts that the check runs, names no corner and gives no note.\n- On unchanged `upstream/main` (`326c938b1`) the pin fails: `50 chords, reach 2: invalid geometry: loop crosses itself`.\n- Mutation: with `Region::new` put back, the pin is red. With `Region::from_slices`, the pin is green.\n\nA probe sweep (not committed) used 24 to 400 chords, 9 reach values and 4 phases.\n\n- Before the fix, 4726 of 13572 cases stopped with the error.\n- After the fix, no case stops.\n- After the fix, 36 cases name corners. Each has 24 to 28 chords and a reach of 8 or 10 mm. Their chord corners are larger than `CORNER_HALF_WIDTH`.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green on the final code.\n\n- `motion lib`: ok.\n- `app:adaptive_zero_margin_island`: ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main` shows one source file and one decision file.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The three tests of the issue with the solidcore mesh. PR B of #917 is not pushed, so the mesh is not available. The owner's diagnosis on the issue says that this fix does not change them.\n- `Milling-test.step` through the solidcore reader. The pin uses a synthetic bore, not the real outline.\n- The heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy`). They did not run. They must run before this PR is flagged ready.\n- A note that changes for a real project. A pocket that showed \"did not run\" can now show a corner note, or no note.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `crates/motion/src/machining2d/unreached.rs`.\n\nPR B of #917 marks the three tests with `known-fail #2849`. This PR does not close the issue, so those markers stay valid.\n\nChangelog: The 2D pocket corner check no longer stops with \"loop crosses itself\" on a bore whose outline has fine chords.\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #2849\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
